  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1127 AM CST Thu Nov 5 2026\n\nThis weekend we'll still struggle to warm up above normal as that \nsystem tracks south of the Panhandles and takes all the precip with \nit.  But high clouds may spread out ahead of it and north of it as \nit moves across west and central Texas this weekend, which is why \nhighs on Saturday and Sunday look to be in the lower to mid 60s.\n\nMonday through Wednesday broad scale high pressure expected to move \nover the the central CONUS leading to near to above normal \ntemperatures and dry conditions.  Still watching the next potential \nfront mid to late next week as a strong back door cold front may \nclip the Panhandles, but there is guidance that suggests it will \nstay further east of our area, and the impact would be minor.  \n\nWeber",
